//! Help topics, searchable from the title bar and the Help window.

pub const TOPICS: [(&str, &str); 26] = [
    ("Getting around", "The tool groups on the left open when you click them. Click a tool to use it. The page is in the middle; the bar above it changes fonts and text style. Every project you have open has a tab at the top; the pages of a card (Front, Inside, Back) have tabs under the page."),
    ("Selecting, moving and resizing", "Click something on the page to select it. Drag it to move it. Drag the small squares to resize: corners change both directions; hold Shift to keep its shape. Drag the round handle above it to turn it; it settles at every 15 degrees unless you hold Alt. Click empty space to deselect. Drag across empty space to select several things."),
    ("Snapping and lining things up", "While you drag, things gently pull toward the page edges, the middle of the page, the printable-area line and the edges and middles of other items. A thin line shows what it lined up with. Hold Alt to move freely. You can change how strong the pull is in Settings. Arrange > Align lines up several selected items; Space Evenly spreads them out."),
    ("Groups", "Select several items (drag across them or Shift-click), then choose Group (Ctrl+G) to move and size them together. Ungroup (Ctrl+Shift+G) separates them again."),
    ("Text and fonts", "Double-click text to change the words. The font list shows each font's look; use the up and down arrow keys to try fonts on your text, then press Enter. The size box takes a number, a scroll of the mouse wheel, or a pick from its list. Fit makes the words fill their box or shape."),
    ("Text in shapes and speech bubbles", "Text in a Shape and Speech Bubbles wrap each line to the shape, so words follow an oval, heart or speech bubble. Left, center and right line up within the shape at each line; top, middle and bottom place the words inside the shape. Fit Text to Its Shape grows or shrinks the words to fill it."),
    ("Headlines", "Headlines are big decorative titles with effects such as blends, shadows and outlines. Arch, Wave and Bulge bend the letters; drag the diamond handle on a selected headline to bend more or less. Letters keep their shape unless you choose Stretch."),
    ("Colors", "Every color button opens the same chooser: basic colors, your last 10 colors, an eyedropper that picks a color from the page, simple sliders for color, strength and light or dark, and color families that go well together. You can copy or paste a color code like #FF8800."),
    ("Pictures", "Type what you're looking for in the box at the top of Pictures on the left and press Enter: Google Images opens, and every picture you click \"+ Add to my project\" on goes straight onto your page. You can also paste a picture (Ctrl+V), drag one in, use a file from your computer, or reuse one from My Art. Art collections you own are under Content Packs in the Pictures window."),
    ("Photo Editor", "Pick a tool along the top. Crop & Turn: drag the corners or edges of the box on the photo. Color and Light & Focus: move the sliders (or scroll over them). Effects: click a look. Cut Out: pick a shape and move or stretch it with its handles, or use the magic wand, draw around something, pick a color, or remove the background; the faded, checkered parts will be cut away. Undo takes back one step; hold Compare to see the photo as it was; Apply keeps the changes."),
    ("Printing", "File > Print shows the printer, paper, copies, quality and which sheets to print, with a preview. Cards print so they fold the right way. The dotted line on the page shows where most printers can't reach; keep important things inside it. Print a test page from the Print window to check your printer's margins."),
    ("Saving and recovery", "PrintCraft saves a safety copy of your open projects every few minutes. If the computer or the app stops unexpectedly, it offers to bring your work back next time. It also reminds you to save before closing."),
    ("Older projects", "File > Open reads older .sig-style project files: the paper size, words, pictures and fonts come in. Their exact positions can't be read yet, so they are placed in order on the page for you to arrange."),
    ("AI pictures", "Tools > AI Pictures can draw a picture from a description using Google's free Gemini service. The first time, it opens Google's page in your browser to get a free key; copy it and paste it into PrintCraft once."),
    ("Keyboard shortcuts", "Ctrl+N new, Ctrl+T new tab, Ctrl+O open, Ctrl+S save, Ctrl+P print, Ctrl+W close tab, Ctrl+Z undo, Ctrl+Y redo, Ctrl+C / X / V copy, cut, paste, Ctrl+D duplicate, Ctrl+G group, Ctrl+Shift+G ungroup, Ctrl+K search, Ctrl+ + and Ctrl+ − zoom the page, Ctrl+0 fits it, Delete removes, arrow keys nudge, F1 help. Sliders follow the mouse wheel, and the arrow keys once clicked."),
    ("Paper size", "File > Page Setup (or click the size at the bottom right) changes the paper: Letter, Legal, Tabloid, A4, A5, A3, photo sizes or your own size, tall or wide. Cards take their panel size from the paper. Tick \"Fit what's on the page\" to scale your design to the new size."),
    ("Updates", "PrintCraft looks for a new version once a day (you can turn this off in Settings). When there is one, it offers to download and install the right kind for your computer. Help > Check for Updates looks right away."),
    ("Reporting a problem or an idea", "Help > Report a Problem or Suggest an Idea opens a short form. PrintCraft adds the details that help find the problem, takes a picture of the window, and opens the report on GitHub with everything filled in (a free GitHub account is needed). Copy the Report puts it on the clipboard for an email instead."),
    ("Ready-made designs", "New Project shows designs to start from for each kind of project (cards, signs, certificates, labels and more), next to Blank. Pick one, then change the words: anything that says Your Name, Date or Place is there to be replaced."),
    ("Calendars", "Choose Calendar in New Project, then the month, how many months, which day weeks start on and the colors. PrintCraft fills in the dates, one page per month, with holidays and the birthdays from your address book. Tools > Calendar Maker fills the open calendar again with other choices."),
    ("Address merge (labels and envelopes)", "Insert Address Merge Field puts in a field like «Address» or «Name». When you print, tick the people to print for: labels get one person each, envelopes one envelope each. The Mailing Labels and Addressed Envelope designs are ready to go."),
    ("Replacing a picture", "Right-click a picture and choose Replace Picture (or use Photo Tools on the left). Pick the new picture from your computer, Google Images or My Art, or paste one: it takes the old picture's place and keeps its frame, shadow and other effects."),
    ("Lines and outlines", "The Line button on the toolbar (three lines) sets how thick lines and outlines are, from none to heavy, and their style: solid, dashed, dotted, double, wavy, zigzag or scribble. It changes what's selected, or what you draw next when nothing is. A line keeps straight when you stretch it; turn it with its round handle."),
    ("Flourishes and dividers", "Decorations > Flourishes & Dividers (or Insert > Flourish or Divider) adds swirls, dividers, vines, underlines, laurels and ribbon banners. The Line color and Fill color buttons color them; Line sets their thickness."),
    ("Moving things between pages", "When every page is shown, drag something from one page and let go over another: it moves to that page, where you dropped it."),
    ("What's coming", "Tables (a grid of cells you can type in, with borders and shading) and Web pages (saving a design as a simple web page) are planned. Exact placement when opening older projects is also on the list."),
];
